<!--
  Hub home — the primary app's index route (`/`).

  Top chrome: <sui-nav-top> with the brand mark (left), and
  the theme picker + account chip (right). The center
  `default` slot is intentionally empty for v0 — the cmdk
  command palette is a real component that will be added
  in a follow-up. The nav-top works without a center slot;
  the app chooses what to fill.

  All chrome components are real primitives from
  `@ship/sui-primitives`. The only thing this page owns is
  the home content below the bar.

  The `{name()}` binding exists so the compiler emits
  `hydrate` on the view's setup return (the compiler only
  emits hydrate when the template binds to scope signals;
  without it the runtime has nothing to call). The signal
  is a no-op constant.
-->
<sui-nav-top>
  <sui-brand-mark slot="brand" href="/" aria-label="Ship home"></sui-brand-mark>
  <sui-theme-picker slot="actions" placement="bottom-end"></sui-theme-picker>
  <sui-account-chip slot="actions"></sui-account-chip>
</sui-nav-top>
<main>
  <h1>{name()}</h1>
  <p>Ship's primary app — ready when you are.</p>
</main>
